{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Mouth to mouth I speak with him.</b> That the prophecy to him comes without his senses being suspended." "<b>And mar'eh.</b> A masculine form, called the illuminating speculum by our Sages of blessed memory (Yevamot 49b)." "<b>And not in riddles.</b> Clear speech without riddle — not like the case of Zechariah (Zechariah 4:5) and others who saw riddles and parables, and the angel said to him, הֲלֹא יָדַעְתָּ מָה הֵמָּה אֵלֶּה, and he said לֹא אֲדֹנִי, and the angel explained the parable to him. And there were some among them who saw the parables and understood them themselves, as in הֵיטַבְתָּ לִרְאוֹת (Jeremiah 1:12). And like Balaam, who said וַיִּשָּׂא מְשָׁלוֹ (Numbers 23:7) — for first he recounted the parable he saw, and afterward explained it." "<b>And the temunah of YHWH he beholds.</b> And all this he grasps along with revelation to him through the Ineffable Name — not like Balaam, who, since he grasped nothing except by way of parable, his grasp was through the name Elohim alone, not through the Ineffable Name." "<b>And why were you not afraid.</b> It cannot be but that this is from evil of heart. For if you thought that I recognize his deeds, then you thought falsely of me — that I desire the wicked, the opposite of what you should have thought: that I would not have granted him this rank except because he is worthy of it. If so, you should have feared to speak against such a man. And if perhaps you thought that I do not recognize his deeds and that you recognize them better than I do — that I thought him worthy but he is not so — then you are thinking even more falsely of YHWH, as they said of blessed memory: זוֹ קָשָׁה מִן הָרִאשׁוֹנָה."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:39:35.459639600Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}